        "id": "1",
        "file": "shop.py",
        "claim": "The migration uses DROP TABLE orders followed by ALTER TABLE orders_new RENAME TO orders, but SQLite's ALTER TABLE rename behavior with foreign-key references is not guaranteed to preserve or correctly rebind the existing order_items FK to the new orders table. This can leave order_items referencing a stale/dropped table or break ON DELETE CASCADE, violating the requirement that order_items still reference orders with cascade working.",
        "severity": "high",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "file": "shop.py",
        "claim": "The code disables foreign keys with PRAGMA foreign_keys=OFF before inserting into orders_new, so invalid customer_id references from the v1 database are not detected or corrected. If the input database has any FK violations, the final PRAGMA foreign_key_check can fail, violating the requirement that FK check be clean.",
        "severity": "medium",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "file": "shop.py",
        "claim": "The code does not restore the original foreign_keys setting if an exception occurs after PRAGMA foreign_keys=OFF has been applied. The finally block only restores isolation_level, so a failed migration can leave the connection with FKs disabled instead of the original setting.",
        "severity": "medium",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "4",
        "file": "shop.py",
        "claim": "The amount conversion can raise OverflowError or ValueError for non-finite SQLite REAL values such as inf or nan, because Decimal(repr(float(amount))) produces Decimal('Infinity') or Decimal('NaN') and int(...) is not valid for those values. This is an unhandled edge case for amount REAL columns.",
        "severity": "medium",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      },
      {
        "id": "5",
        "file": "shop.py",
        "claim": "The code assumes schema_version exists and contains exactly one row. If the database is malformed or missing schema_version, version(conn) can raise an exception instead of doing nothing or handling the migration safely.",
        "severity": "low",
        "status": "dropped",
        "investigation": "no deterministic repro; dropped (not repaired)"
      }
